{
  "sn35.103:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.103 ",
  "sn35.103:0.2": "10. The Sixes ",
  "sn35.103:0.3": "About Uddaka ",
  "sn35.103:1.1": "“Mendicants, Uddaka son of Rāma used to say: ",
  "sn35.103:1.2": "‘Hereupon, ever the knowledge master! ",
  "sn35.103:1.3": "Hereupon, ever the conqueror of all! ",
  "sn35.103:1.4": "Hereupon, ever the undug ",
  "sn35.103:1.5": "boil’s root was dug out by me!’ ",
  "sn35.103:1.6": "Even though Uddaka son of Rāma was no knowledge master, he said ‘I’m a knowledge master.’ Though he was no conqueror of all, he said ‘I’m conqueror of all.’ And though the boil’s root was not dug out, he said ‘I’ve dug out the boil’s root.’ ",
  "sn35.103:1.7": "A mendicant might rightly say here: ",
  "sn35.103:1.8": "‘Hereupon, ever the knowledge master! ",
  "sn35.103:1.9": "Hereupon, ever the conqueror of all! ",
  "sn35.103:1.10": "Hereupon, ever the undug ",
  "sn35.103:1.11": "boil’s root is dug out!’ ",
  "sn35.103:2.1": "And how is someone a knowledge master? ",
  "sn35.103:2.2": "It’s when a mendicant truly understands the six fields of contact’s origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape. ",
  "sn35.103:2.3": "That’s how a mendicant is a knowledge master. ",
  "sn35.103:3.1": "And how is a mendicant a conqueror of all? ",
  "sn35.103:3.2": "It’s when a mendicant comes to be freed by not grasping after truly understanding the six fields of contact’s origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape. ",
  "sn35.1